{
  "tutorial": {
    "id": 4604,
    "version": 1,
    "type": "course",
    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "python",
    "title": "Managing Package Versions",
    "descriptionContent": "Control dependency versions and update packages.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "Python learners who can install packages from requirements.txt.",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17792,
        "title": "Why Versions Matter",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Same Project, Different Result",
            "id": 151810,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Everyone who runs the table project uses <code>requirements.txt</code> to install the same set of dependencies.</p><p>However, the package can change. If you (or someone else) come back later, the installed package may have changed, which could cause issues.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Packages Change",
            "id": 151811,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Packages change over time as developers work on them. New releases can include fixes and features.</p><p>They can also deprecate old behavior or introduce breaking changes.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"release_history.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"0.8.10: fixes\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"0.9.0: features and deprecations\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Versions Affect Behavior",
            "id": 151812,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When our environment uses version <code>0.8.10</code>, and we have tested this specific version. It's a good idea to specify that in <code>requirements.txt</code>.</p><p>Specify the version by adding <code>==</code> and the version number directly next to the package name.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate==0.8.10\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>, followed by <code>0.8.10</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Versions Affect Behavior - Copy",
            "id": 151813,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>An exact pin uses <code>==</code> to require one package version.</p><p>Add the missing characters to pin version 0.8.10 for the package <code>tabulate</code>.<br /></p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate==0.8.10\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Recreate the Environment",
            "id": 151814,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We don't have to specify a version number, but if we do, <code>pip</code> will ensure that whenever we run <code>pip install</code>, it installs the correct version.</p><p>This is useful whenever we want to run the project from scratch and avoid compatibility issues.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install -r requirements.txt\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When <code>requirements.txt</code> pins a version, installing from that file asks pip for that exact release.</p><p>This is useful whenever we want to run the project from scratch and avoid compatibility issues.</p><p>Recreate the environment from <code>requirements.txt</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install -r requirements.txt\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"14\" /><option startIndex=\"15\" endIndex=\"31\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"tabulate\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"import\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"requirements.py\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>, <code>-r</code>, and finally <code>requirements.txt</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Pin Another Package",
            "id": 151817,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Pin <code>requests</code> to exactly version <code>2.32.3</code> so teammates install the same release.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests==2.23.3\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>requests</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>2.23.3</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Pin <code>requests</code> to exactly version <code>2.32.3</code> so teammates install the same release.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests==\" /><text value=\"2.32\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\".\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>requests</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>2.32.3</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Recall Package Changes",
            "id": 151815,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which package change could cause the old project's behavior to stop working?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A breaking change in a new release<br /></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Installing the same exact release again</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A breaking change in a new release<br />.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Your project calls a package function with two inputs. A new release accepts only one. What should you check before updating?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Whether the project must change its call to work with the new release.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Only whether the package name stayed the same; its calls must still work.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Nothing, because a newer version always preserves existing calls.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Whether the project must change its call to work with the new release.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Identify the Version",
            "id": 151816,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which exact tabulate version will pip install from this requirements file?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate==0.9.0\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">0.9.0</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">0.8.10</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick 0.9.0.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You change the file to <code>tabulate==0.8.10</code>. Version <code>0.9.0</code> is also available. Which version does installing from the changed file request?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate==0.9.0\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>0.8.10</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>0.9.0</code>, because it is newer.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Either version, because both belong to tabulate.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>0.8.10</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Pin Another Package 2",
            "id": 151818,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Using <code>==</code>, pin <code>numpy</code> to exactly version <code>2.5.2</code> so teammates, AI agents, and future you install the same release.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"numpy==2.5.2\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"5\" endIndex=\"7\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17793,
        "title": "Ranges and Deliberate Updates",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Allow Compatible Updates",
            "id": 151819,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When working with <code>pip</code>, an exact pin keeps one release, but it doesn't allow newer fixes to install automatically.</p><p>A version range can allow selected updates while setting limits. Let's dive into more advanced ways to set accepted versions.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Set a Lower Bound",
            "id": 151821,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With <code>&gt;=</code>, we set a lower bound. It allows versions above a specified version.</p><p>Complete the lower-bound operator in <code>requirements.txt</code> to allow versions 0.8 or newer.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate&gt;=0.8\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&gt;=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Set an Upper Bound",
            "id": 151822,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With <code>&lt;</code>, we set an upper bound. It excludes the specified versions and anything newer.</p><p>Complete the upper-bound operator to exclude versions 1 or newer.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate&lt;1.0\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"9\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>&lt;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Read the Whole Range",
            "id": 151823,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With a comma, we can join an upper-bound and a lower-bound rule to allow only versions in a specific range.</p><p>Complete the code to allow versions from 0.8 up to, but not including, 1.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate&gt;=0.8,&lt;1\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"14\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>,</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A comma joins two version rules. The <code>&lt;</code> rule excludes its boundary and all newer versions.</p><p>For <code>tabulate</code>, allow version <code>0.8</code> and newer, but exclude version <code>1</code> and above.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate&gt;=0.8,&lt;1\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"14\" /><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>tabulate</code>, followed by <code>&gt;=</code>, and finally <code>,</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare a Pin and a Range",
            "id": 151824,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>requirements.txt</code>, we can specify an exact version or a range for each package.</p><p>Ensure that <code>numpy</code> always uses version 2.5.2, and specify a range for <code>tabulate</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"numpy==2.5.2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"tabulate&gt;=0.8,&lt;1\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"29\" /><option startIndex=\"5\" endIndex=\"12\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==2.5.2</code>, followed by <code>&gt;=0.8</code>, and finally <code>,&lt;1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>requirements.txt</code>, we can specify an exact version or a range for each package.</p><p>Pin <code>numpy</code> to <code>2.5.2</code>. Allow <code>tabulate</code> from <code>0.8</code> inclusive to below <code>1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"numpy==2.5.2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"tabulate&gt;=0.8,&lt;1\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"5\" endIndex=\"7\" /><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"28\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>, followed by <code>&gt;=</code>, and finally <code>&lt;</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Choose for the Goal",
            "id": 151825,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the code to use an exact-pin operator.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate==0.8\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Change One Dependency",
            "id": 151826,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Allow only versions below 0.8 for the given package.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate&lt;0.8\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"9\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&lt;</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Interpret a Range",
            "id": 151827,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which statement matches this bounded version range?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests&gt;=1.2,&lt;2\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Install version 1.2 or newer, but lower than 2</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Install only version 1.2</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Install version 1.2 or newer, but lower than 2.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You keep the shown range. A fresh environment can choose version <code>1.1</code>, <code>1.2</code>, or <code>2</code>. Which one satisfies both rules?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests&gt;=1.2,&lt;2\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>1.2</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>1.1</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>2</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>1.2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Write a Bounded Range",
            "id": 151828,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Set the range so <code>requests</code> can use version 2.30 or newer, but stays below 3.<br /></p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests&gt;=2.30,&lt;3\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;2,&lt;=3\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&gt;=2.30,&lt;3</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Set the range so <code>requests</code> can use version 2.30 or newer, but stays below 3.<br/></p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"requests&gt;=2.30,&lt;3\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"15\" /><option startIndex=\"15\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&gt;=</code>, followed by <code>,</code>, and finally <code>&lt;</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
